;; =======================================================
;; THE RASTER BEAM (BLITZ MODE)
;; =======================================================
;; The beam's line and the lines between two readings, for everything that times itself by the
;; beam: the frame time report (sparkydave.timing-marks.blitz.ab3, .frametime.blitz.ab3), the
;; sound's split of it (SoundTimeMark{}, sparkydave.sound.blitz.ab3) and the palette's wait. In a
;; file of its own, included before the sound, so the standalone sound program (proofs/sound-engine.ab3), which
;; compiles the sound files and little else, can include it too: one copy of the beam read.

;; The raster beam's line: the custom chip VPOSR and VHPOSR read together, bit 16 is V8, bits 8
;; to 15 are V0 to V7. Masked before dividing, because bit 31 is a flag and the long is negative.
;; The frame time report's marks (here and sparkydave.frametime.blitz.ab3) and the palette's
;; wait use it.
Function.l RasterLine{}
  rawPosition.l = Peek.l($dff004)
  Function Return(rawPosition AND $1ff00)/256
End Function

; Lines from one mark to the next, corrected for one beam wrap.
Function.l SegmentLines{fromLine.l, toLine.l, frameLines.l}
  segment.l = toLine - fromLine
  If segment < 0 Then segment = segment + frameLines
  Function Return segment
End Function

;; END OF THE RASTER BEAM (BLITZ MODE)
